  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 107 PM MDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday...West-southwest flow continues across the \nregion through mid week, providing for dry conditions and warm \ntemps, with highs on Wednesday 5-10 degrees above normal. Another \nfast-moving shortwave crossing the Rockies Wed will push a weak cold \nfront south into eastern CO early Thu, dropping afternoon highs Thu \nby about 5 degrees.\n\nFriday through Sunday...Broad Pacific trough, with a low center just \noff the Pacific NW coast, will start to strengthen and drop south \nalong the coastline Thu, which will by Fri produce deep southwest \nflow across the Desert Sw and the Four Corners. This will once again \ndraw moisture up into the western half of the state, leading to \ncooler and more active weather into the weekend, as well as \naccumulating mt snow starting Fri night. There are some variations \nin the long range solutions between models, so this is a little \nearly getting into specifics. Moore",
